<article class="tgp-post" id="post-4702">
	<h2>MTG Drafts at TGP in 2026</h2>	<div class="tgp-date-and-time">
		<div class="tgp-date"></div>
		<div class="tgp-time">8:08 am</div>
	</div>
			<div class="tgp-categories">
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/board-certified/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					Board Certified				</a>
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/tgp-events/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					TGP Events				</a>
					</div>
		<hr />
	<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="4706" data-permalink="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/05/26/mtg-drafts-at-tgp-in-2026/draft/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/draft.png?fit=851%2C315&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="851,315" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;}" data-image-title="draft" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/draft.png?fit=640%2C237&amp;ssl=1" class="aligncenter wp-image-4706 size-full" src="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/draft.png?resize=640%2C237&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="640" height="237" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/draft.png?w=851&amp;ssl=1 851w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/draft.png?resize=300%2C111&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/draft.png?resize=768%2C284&amp;ssl=1 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></p>
<hr />
<p>The Gathering Place is changing how we run our weekly Draft events for Magic: The Gathering starting in June of 2026, and we&#8217;re excited to outline the roll out of our new Draft plans for any established enjoyers of Limited play and any newer folks who&#8217;d like to give cracking packs and playing cards a go.</p>
<p>Friday Night Magic is a long-standing tradition in the MTG community, and here at TGP we want to do our best to continue cultivating a strong Magic community. Part of that is making sure Friday Night Magic (FNM) is a big deal with a firm focus on what’s currently happening in the game.</p>
<p>Starting in June, Friday Night Magic Drafts will be whatever we have in stock that’s the newest Standard set in MTG. Price for entry will reflect that, as will pack prizing and the promos provided by Wizards. We’re going to kick FNM firmly into gear when it comes to running events live and direct with what’s fresh off the presses.</p>
<p>Of course, The Gathering Place doesn’t just run MTG Draft events on Fridays — we’ve been hosting Sunday Draft events for quite a while! Since Fridays are now exclusively for what’s new, hot and happening with MTG we’ve opened up some space for fun stuff on Sundays! To prove the point, here’s what we’re drafting in June on Sundays:</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>LOTR / Week 1 – $50 , 24 player cap</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Conspiracy: Take The Crown / Week 2 – $35, 24 player cap</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Ikoria / Week 3 – $35, no cap</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Mystery Booster / Week 4 – $55, 16 player cap</em></p>
<p>Prizing for these TGP Draft events on Sundays will also be handled differently. Instead of packs, prizing will be given in the form of store credit. $10 per win for anyone with a winning record across three Swiss rounds, with a Foil Promo Pack for the top / undefeated player.</p>
<p>You&#8217;ll see signups for these Sunday MTG Drafts posted online over on the <span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://the-gathering-place.mybigcommerce.com/event-calendar/">preregistration section of the TGP Online Shop</a></span> soon. Thanks for reading, and we look forward to hosting some great Draft tournaments in the immediate future!</p>
</article><!-- #post-4702 -->                
<article class="tgp-post" id="post-4669">
	<h2>TGP Dispatch: 5/19/26</h2>	<div class="tgp-date-and-time">
		<div class="tgp-date">May 19, 2026</div>
		<div class="tgp-time">4:44 pm</div>
	</div>
			<div class="tgp-categories">
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/weekly-annoucements/tgp-dispatch/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					TGP Dispatch				</a>
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/weekly-annoucements/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					Weekly Annoucements				</a>
					</div>
		<hr />
	<p style="text-align: center;"><span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/events-page/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em><strong>TGP Events Page</strong></em></a></span></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jut0TLxHDOo1fQkL91lKqt-EmDBdwZ4QsUhhPHToCLY/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em><strong><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Monthly Calendar for The Gathering Place in Google Sheets</span></strong></em></a></p>
<hr />
<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="4673" data-permalink="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/05/19/tgp-dispatch-5-19-26/dispatch-template-8/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-3.png?fit=851%2C315&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="851,315" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="dispatch template" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-3.png?fit=640%2C237&amp;ssl=1" class="aligncenter wp-image-4673 size-full" src="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-3.png?resize=640%2C237&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="640" height="237" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-3.png?w=851&amp;ssl=1 851w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-3.png?resize=300%2C111&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-3.png?resize=768%2C284&amp;ssl=1 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></p>
<hr />
<p>This week at The Gathering Place, we&#8217;ve got Flesh and Blood getting some love on the calendar, a whole lot of One Piece action, and a few events helping us close out May strong before we crash headlong into June 2026!</p>
<p>The FAB Team Trios event on Saturday, paired with a projector-in-the-back-of-TGP watch party for the Prague tournament, and Sunday that cruises straight into the One Piece TCG Extra Grand Battle &#8212; which, if you haven&#8217;t heard, if One Piece&#8217;s way of saying &#8220;we&#8217;re not going anywhere&#8221; by introducing a historic + non-rotating format.</p>
<p>A little further out in the future, we&#8217;ve got a new FAB set prerelease, an MTG Old School cash tournament, more Riftbound competitive space, and a great deal more. But, before we get ahead of ourselves, here&#8217;s the breakdowns for the rest of the events in the month, straight from the <span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/events-page/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TGP events page</a></span>.</p>
<hr />
<h3>Flesh and Blood Team Trios Tournament &amp; World Premiere Prague Watch Party</h3>
<p><em>Saturday, May 23, 12:00 p.m.</em></p>
<p>It&#8217;s an all-out FAB brawl at The Gathering Place! Saturday, May 23, starting at noon, we&#8217;re running a Team Trios tournament sure to knock the socks clean off all who dare step into the ring.</p>
<p>$20 buy in per player, each member of the team must use a different hero, prizing based on attendance. All three matches will be Classic Constructed, and we&#8217;ll have a FAB judge on hand. We&#8217;ll also tie this into putting the World Premiere FAB matches on the TVs over the tournament tables, so come hang!</p>
<p><a href="https://fabtcg.com/locator/the-gathering-place/"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
<h3>One Piece TCG Extra Grand Battle</h3>
<p><em>Sunday, May 24, 1:00 p.m.</em></p>
<p>Congratulations to One Piece for having made it into the hallowed halls of TCGs that need to introduce a historic format. As cards rotate out and the current meta shifts, One Piece Extra Grand Battle is a non-rotating all-time bangers way to play. TGP is running a tournament for EGB on Sunday, May 24, at 1:00 p.m. with $20 entry per player, pack and promo prizing, and the tournament will continue until there is a single undefeated player, an Extra Grand Champion!</p>
<p><a href="https://www.bandai-tcg-plus.com/event/6429173" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
<h3>Flesh and Blood: Omens of the Third Age Prerelease</h3>
<p><em>Friday, May 29, 7:30 p.m.</em></p>
<p>A new FAB release, a new Friday stacked with stuff!</p>
<p><a href="https://fabtcg.com/locator/the-gathering-place/"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
<h3>MTG Old School Cash Tournament (MTGPunks Series)</h3>
<p><em>Saturday, May 30, 12:00 p.m.</em></p>
<p>The MTGPunks tournament series at TGP is a monthly rotating cash tournament series of community-driven and fan-favorite formats for Magic.</p>
<p>May is Old School&#8217;s turn in the sun. We&#8217;re talking $30 entry! All Buy in going back into the prize pool! Old School at The Gathering Place, played using the <span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://www.eternalcentral.com/oldschool/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Eternal Central guidelines</a>! </span></p>
<p>Play Magic the way that Richard Garfield intended; with a nostalgic card pool from Alpha to Fallen Empires—where every deck is a time machine! Relive the aesthetics and power of iconic cards and strategic depth from &#8217;93-&#8217;94, all while embracing the charm of old-school gameplay.</p>
<p><a href="https://the-gathering-place.mybigcommerce.com/mtg-old-school-cash-tournament/"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
<h3>Riftbound Summoner&#8217;s Skirmish</h3>
<p><em>Sunday, May 31, 1:00 p.m.</em></p>
<p>Riftbound continues to be a hit at TGP and beyond, and we&#8217;ll be closing out May with another Summoner&#8217;s Skirmish!</p>
<p>This tournament will be run at a competitive rules enforcement level. 32 player maximum, $20 entry per player, Swiss rounds followed by a cut to top. If you&#8217;ve ever wanted to give serious competitive Riftbound play a shot, now&#8217;s your chance!</p>
<p><a href="https://locator.riftbound.uvsgames.com/events/409434"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
<p>With that done, let&#8217;s start looking into the future &#8212; specifically, the month of June! There&#8217;s already all the month&#8217;s events planned out and listed on the TGP events page, and you can expect to see a monthly roundup as we get closer to the end of May. But there&#8217;s two big-picture items well worth covering this early in a Dispatch: first, we&#8217;re changing how MTG Draft happens at The Gathering Place and, second, we&#8217;re formally setting sail with Castaway Commander League at the end of June!</p>
<p><span style="color: #ff0000;"><em><strong>About Draft</strong></em></span></p>
<p>We&#8217;re going to change up how MTG Draft events happen at The Gathering Place. It&#8217;s a long-standing tradition for Friday Night Magic (FNM) to be a big deal with a firm focus on what&#8217;s currently happening in the game, and we&#8217;re going to adjust our schedule to reflect that.</p>
<p>Starting in June, Friday Night Magic Drafts will be whatever we have in stock that&#8217;s the newest Standard set in MTG. Price for entry will reflect that, as will pack prizing and the promos provided by Wizards. We&#8217;re going to kick FNM firmly into gear when it comes to running events live and direct with what&#8217;s fresh off the presses.</p>
<p>Of course, The Gathering Place doesn&#8217;t just run MTG Draft events on Fridays &#8212; we&#8217;ve been hosting Sunday Draft events for quite a while! Since Fridays are now exclusively for what&#8217;s new, hot and happening with MTG we&#8217;ve opened up some space for fun stuff on Sundays! To prove the point, here&#8217;s what we&#8217;re drafting in June on Sundays:</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>LOTR Week 1 – $50 , 24 player cap</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Conspiracy Week 2 – $35, 24 player cap</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Ikoria Week 3 – $35, no cap</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Mystery Booster Week 4 – $55, 16 player cap</em></p>
<p>Prizing for these TGP Draft events on Sundays will also be handled differently. Instead of packs, prizing will be given in the form of store credit. $10 per win for anyone with a winning record across three Swiss rounds, with a Foil Promo Pack for the top / undefeated player.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ff0000;"><em><strong>About Castaway Commander League</strong></em></span></p>
<p>Last year&#8217;s &#8220;Summer Session&#8221; of TGP&#8217;s signature Commander League was where Commander League X and beyond began to find footing, and this year&#8217;s Summer League is going to keep up the trend we&#8217;ve seen through 2026 of League experimentation and innovation. To that end, we&#8217;re excited and delighted to announce: Castaway League!</p>
<p>Picture this: you&#8217;re marooned on an island, with nothing but the few Magic cards you were able to save from the shipwreck. Over the course of Castaway League, you&#8217;ll take those humble beginnings and turn them into a tournament powerhouse alongside (and occasionally against) your fellow castaways. Eight weeks, two tournaments, events and challenges à la Survivor reality TV nonsense, it&#8217;s gonna be a whole thing. It&#8217;s going to be Castaway League. It starts on June 30, and we&#8217;ll see you on The Island!</p>
<p><span style="color: #ffcc00;"><em><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2024/05/14/castaway-league-26-at-the-gathering-place/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Click here for our full post about Castaway Commander League, with all the details about the event</a></em></span></p>
<p>As always, thanks for reading this week&#8217;s Dispatch. As temperatures and humidity levels rise and the weather outside becomes progressively more true to North Carolina&#8217;s temperate rainforest classification, we&#8217;re continue to be your air-conditioned indoor haven for games galore. See you around!</p>
</article><!-- #post-4669 -->                
<article class="tgp-post" id="post-4643">
	<h2>Castaway League &#8217;26 at The Gathering Place</h2>	<div class="tgp-date-and-time">
		<div class="tgp-date">May 17, 2026</div>
		<div class="tgp-time">1:13 pm</div>
	</div>
			<div class="tgp-categories">
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/commander-league/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					Commander League				</a>
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/commander-league/summer-session/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					Summer Session				</a>
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/tgp-events/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					TGP Events				</a>
					</div>
		<hr />
	<p>Last year, we laid down a solid foundation – Commander League: Summer Session was a surprise smash hit, and became the inspiration for so much more we’ve been doing at The Gathering Place since.</p>
<p>To that end, for 2026, we are delighted to introduce something entirely new for the Summer League at TGP:</p>
<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="4644" data-permalink="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/05/17/castaway-league-26-at-the-gathering-place/castaway-league/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?fit=2600%2C1000&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="2600,1000" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="castaway league" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?fit=640%2C246&amp;ssl=1" class="aligncenter wp-image-4644 size-full" src="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?resize=640%2C246&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="640" height="246" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?w=2600&amp;ssl=1 2600w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?resize=300%2C115&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?resize=1024%2C394&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?resize=768%2C295&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?resize=1536%2C591&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?resize=2048%2C788&amp;ssl=1 2048w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?w=1280&amp;ssl=1 1280w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/castaway-league.png?w=1920&amp;ssl=1 1920w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>You signed up for Cruise: The Gathering, a promised couple weeks of fun in the sun and sand with some of the world’s foremost players of Magic aboard the SS. Garfield. Islands both Tropical and Volcanic, lush jungles and white sand, it was all lined up to be the perfect summer.</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Unfortunately for you, the summer you expected is not the summer you’ll experience.</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>A sudden Thousand-Year storm at sea, paired with a series of mechanical malfunctions below decks, has left you and your traveling cohort marooned! After being adrift aimlessly for the better part of three days, The SS Garfield has now run aground on an uncharted island. Listing dangerously and unsafe to inhabit any longer – to say nothing of unpleasant, you know it smells crazy in there – all hands and all passengers have abandoned ship to seek refuge elsewhere.</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>The rescue party, if it ever arrives, is surely weeks away.</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>In the meantime, you’ve got to do the best you can to survive. Both on your own, and as part of the burgeoning castaway society operating by the rules of a shonen anime. Power and position, privilege and progress all hinge on one thing: playing MTG. It&#8217;s up to you to have the wits, the skill, the heart to prevail on The Island.</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>You were able to save just 11 cards through this ordeal : your favorite Commander, and 10 others. From there, your only hope of surviving the island hinges on scavenging supplies from the shipwreck of the Garfield, dangerous forays into the depths of the jungle, salvaging resources and playing pitched games of Commander where the winner decides how the spoils are split.</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Eight weeks. Two tournaments. Castaway League.</em></p>
<p>Sure, that’s a fun dramatic scene-setting introduction and all, but here’s the actual structure for this summer’s Castaway League.</p>
<p>Entry is $45 per player, and entry is all-inclusive for beginning materials and both tournaments.</p>
<p>Each player will provide 11 cards on their own: a Commander, and 10 spells and/or lands as a base for their deck. Cards classed as Game Changers, as well as cards present on the Banned and Restricted lists, are not permitted. Players must submit their list of 11 cards for review + approval before they will be allowed to participate in Castaway League <span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://forms.gle/R8Y3UW4Tw2S2guE1A">via this signup form</a></span>. The Commander you start with is not required to be the Commander you keep forever, flexibility is paramount in a League environment and The Pivot is always possible.</p>
<p>At the start of Castaway League, each player will receive a pack of 100 Dragon Shield sleeves, six booster packs of randomly-determined MTG sets from TGP stock, and a randomized selection of evenly color-distributed MTG cards assembled into a roughly 50-card Supply Crate. Resources are scarce, so trading within League will be more important than ever while you’re marooned on The Island.</p>
<p>Castaway League players will be eligible to pick up one traditional Commander League pack slot per week, permitting them to specifically choose / purchase an MTG booster pack. From there, all other League pack pulls will be from the Magic Hole (a box of random packs from TGP stock both off the shelves and from the Distro Dungeon). Each pull from the Magic Hole will cost $13, and each player can scavenge for resources from the Magic Hole a maximum of three (3) times per visit to TGP.</p>
<p>Additional “resource gathering” will be accomplished both individually and together through weekly goals, trials, and challenges. Castaway League players can expect to be split into teams, vote on certain outcomes / events, and other reality show adjacent nonsense. You’ll be spinning wheels, completing scavenger hunts, and more.</p>
<p>Commander meetup days will remain on Tuesdays, Thursday and Saturdays. Castaway League will have a separate signup sheet from Commander Meetup, and players choosing to play within Castaway League on any given night will need to sign up / in to receive credit + recognition for their attendance and gameplay performance. League decks, as always, must remain at The Gathering Place for the duration of the event. Speaking of duration:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Tuesday, June 30</strong> – Castaway League begins</li>
<li><strong>Saturday, July 25</strong> – Mid-League Tournament</li>
<li><strong>Saturday, August 22</strong> – Castaway League Finale Tournament</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="color: #ff0000;">To summarize: </span></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Entry is $45 per player, each player will provide 11 cards of their own choice and begin with sleeves + a starter kit from TGP. </em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Packs can be purchased weekly through two main methods: pack slots and random pulls, and there will be additional opportunities for pack slots and Castaway League bonuses through participation in League events / challenges / milestones throughout the season.</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Meetups are Tuesdays, Thursdays and Saturdays, players are not required to attend every single meetup to participate in League. The Mid-League tournament is on 7/25 and the Finale Tournament is on 8/22. </em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>If you have any questions or would like any clarifications, don&#8217;t hesitate to get in touch with Victor either on the TGP Discord or via email (<span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="mailto:victor@thegatheringplacegames.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">victor@thegatheringplacegames.com</a></span>). League is for anybody who wants to participate!</em></p>
<p>That’s a lot of dry bones, but hopefully you get the gist of what we’re going for here! Castaway League is somehow both lower, and higher, stakes than any League before it. We&#8217;re getting goofy with it, and prioritizing fun weird stuff &#8220;it could only happen in Commander&#8221; type MTG in a big way. You’ll be trading cards week over week, making treasure out of trash, and steadily assembling a deck with the juice to carry you to victory and crown you Castaway Royalty – provided you get off The Island at all.</p>
<p>In terms of prizing, we’re still getting it all together – you can expect to see some fun + on-theme alters, Secret Lair printings, boxes of boosters, and perhaps even something more….<em> Reserved</em> if things REALLY get popping for Castaway League signups. You can <a href="https://forms.gle/R8Y3UW4Tw2S2guE1A" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="color: #ffcc00;">preregister for League starting today</span></a>, and we’ll see you on the beach!</p>
</article><!-- #post-4643 -->                
<article class="tgp-post" id="post-4495">
	<h2>COMMANDERJAM 2026 (Saturday, May 16)</h2>	<div class="tgp-date-and-time">
		<div class="tgp-date">May 16, 2026</div>
		<div class="tgp-time">11:00 am</div>
	</div>
			<div class="tgp-categories">
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/big-news/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					Big News				</a>
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/board-certified/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					Board Certified				</a>
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/tgp-events/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					TGP Events				</a>
					</div>
		<hr />
	<p><em>(this post has been edited from its original version, since Commanderjam is happening NOW. if you&#8217;d like to take a look at the <span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/tgps-parking/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TGP Parking Guide, it&#8217;s right here</a></span>.)</em></p>
<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="4505" data-permalink="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/05/16/commanderjam-2026-saturday-may-16/1-13/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?fit=1080%2C1350&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="1080,1350" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="1" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?fit=640%2C800&amp;ssl=1" class="aligncenter wp-image-4505 size-large" src="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?resize=640%2C800&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="640" height="800" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?resize=819%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 819w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?resize=240%2C300&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?resize=768%2C960&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?w=1080&amp;ssl=1 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></p>
<p>The second annual Commanderjam is set to include a Commander Legends draft, special pods for Two-Headed Giant EDH as well as a return of Planechase, a huge convention table setup run by none other than the Mohawk Man himself, artists and friends of the shop, door prizes all day, Alpha Pie pizza slinging slices from the downstairs service window, another round of deckbuilding workshops &#8212; it&#8217;s all here, it&#8217;s all happening, it&#8217;s all COMMANDERJAM and it&#8217;s on <strong>Saturday, May 16</strong>!</p>
<p>We&#8217;ve got a luxury variant of the Magic Hole, we&#8217;ll have discounts and deals all day long in celebration of Magic&#8217;s most popular format, there&#8217;s a lot happening in-store all day long!</p>
<p>Signup sheets for each event will be posted at the bar, all events are first-come, first served. We&#8217;ll be firing pods as we get four players to play, so don&#8217;t worry too much about timing!</p>
<p>Folks who filled out the Commanderjam Form prior to the event will already be listed / included on each sheet.</p>
<p>Most events don&#8217;t have a cap involved! It&#8217;s more about podding players together, and we&#8217;ve got a bunch of table space and the entire day reserved for nothing but MTG. We&#8217;re trying to make as much space as possible for folks to play Magic&#8217;s most popular format, all day!</p>
<p>Here&#8217;s a the schedule of events:</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>11:00 a.m. —</strong> TGP opens</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>12:00 p.m. —</strong> Commander Legends Commander Draft event (<a href="https://magic.wizards.com/en/formats/commander-limited" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Commander Draft guidelines according to WotC</a>)</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>$55 entry, best of 1, single elimination. Event prizing to pods, additional prizing to winners + Top. <a href="https://topdeck.gg/event/commander-jam-2k26-legends-draft">Registration for the event is on TopDeck, right here!</a></em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>2:00 p.m. —</strong> 2HG and Planechase pods in-person signups open, first door prize drawings of the day!</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong> 2:30 p.m. —</strong> 2HG and Planechase pods formally fire</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>3:00 p.m. —</strong> Door prize drawings continue for everyone in-store, Commander pods form + fire as table space allows with special Commanderjam prize support. For folks interested in playing unaltered preconstructed decks and exhibition cEDH games, we’ll pair you up accordingly!</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Space on Commanderjam Saturday might be a little tougher to come by, and TGP staff are going to prioritize finding seating for groups playing MTG. We’re going to make sure there’s some additional space outside on the Alpha Pie patio for anyone who’d like to hang outdoors and play MTG al fresco, as well!</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>4:00 p.m. —</strong> Deckbuilding Workshop sessions with Preston “Ironworks” Stevenson + friends open on a first-come, first-served basis. Possible guest-star inclusions for cEDH learn-to-play and other topics!</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>For any Alpha Pie aficionados, a note from the <span style="color: #ff0000;">Pizza Lord</span> himself:</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">tomorrow, during Commanderjam, Alpha Pie will be offering a special slice: ExtraExtraExtra Pep (it&#8217;s more pepperoni than you bargained for, I&#8217;m trying to tell you) also, a limited edition brand new hot sauce, straight out the kitchen</span></em></p>
<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="4506" data-permalink="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/05/16/commanderjam-2026-saturday-may-16/2-13/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2.png?fit=1080%2C1350&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="1080,1350" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="2" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2.png?fit=640%2C800&amp;ssl=1" class="aligncenter wp-image-4506 size-large" src="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2.png?resize=640%2C800&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="640" height="800" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2.png?resize=819%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 819w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2.png?resize=240%2C300&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2.png?resize=768%2C960&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2.png?w=1080&amp;ssl=1 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></p>
</article><!-- #post-4495 -->                
<article class="tgp-post" id="post-4622">
	<h2>TGP Dispatch: 5/12/26</h2>	<div class="tgp-date-and-time">
		<div class="tgp-date">May 12, 2026</div>
		<div class="tgp-time">5:38 pm</div>
	</div>
			<div class="tgp-categories">
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/weekly-annoucements/tgp-dispatch/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					TGP Dispatch				</a>
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/weekly-annoucements/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					Weekly Annoucements				</a>
					</div>
		<hr />
	<p style="text-align: center;"><span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/events-page/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em><strong>TGP Events Page</strong></em></a></span></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jut0TLxHDOo1fQkL91lKqt-EmDBdwZ4QsUhhPHToCLY/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em><strong><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Monthly Calendar for The Gathering Place in Google Sheets</span></strong></em></a></p>
<hr />
<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="4636" data-permalink="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/05/12/tgp-dispatch-5-12-26/dispatch-template-7/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-2.png?fit=851%2C315&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="851,315" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="dispatch template" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-2.png?fit=640%2C237&amp;ssl=1" class="aligncenter wp-image-4636 size-full" src="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-2.png?resize=640%2C237&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="640" height="237" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-2.png?w=851&amp;ssl=1 851w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-2.png?resize=300%2C111&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template-2.png?resize=768%2C284&amp;ssl=1 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<hr />
<p>This week at The Gathering Place: with just a little over a month left to go in spring and summer months taking shape for the shop, there&#8217;s so much fun and cool stuff on the horizon for your local game store / bar / pizza place / hangout!</p>
<p>Which, speaking of things in close proximity re: time</p>
<p><span style="color: #ffcc00;"><strong><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/04/21/commanderjam-2026-saturday-may-16/">COMMANDERJAM is this Saturday</a></strong>!</span></p>
<p>Finally, it&#8217;s here! The second annual Commanderjam is this Saturday, 5/16! It&#8217;s been talked about, hyped up, ballyhooed, fretted over, and it&#8217;s time at last! Here&#8217;s a real quick rundown, in case you don&#8217;t know what we&#8217;re talking about.</p>
<p>This Saturday is Commaderjam, an annual all-day celebration of Magic: The Gathering &#8212; and, specifically, the EDH / Commander archetype &#8212; at The Gathering Place in Chapel Hill, North Carolina.</p>
<p>A Commander Legends draft, special pods for Two-Headed Giant EDH as well as a return of Planechase, a convention table setup run by none other than the Mohawk Man himself, artists and friends of the shop, door prizes all day, Alpha Pie pizza rockin’ out the downstairs service window, another round of deckbuilding workshops — it’s all here, it’s all happening, it’s all COMMANDERJAM and it’s on <strong>Saturday, May 16</strong>!</p>
<p><em>If you’re interested in participating in this year’s COMMANDERJAM, <a href="https://forms.gle/j6UDuNVu3YwCC1Ve7" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="color: #ffcc00;">check out our form right here!</span></a> Answer some questions, sign up for specialty events, and get your name on the list early for the biggest and best door prizes of the day!</em></p>
<p>We’re also working on bringing back some old friends: the Wheel of Fortune, the Magic Hole, we’ll have discounts and deals all day long in celebration of Magic’s most popular format.</p>
<p>Here’s a schedule of events:</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>11:00 a.m. —</strong> TGP opens</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>12:00 p.m. —</strong> Commander Legends Commander Draft event (<a href="https://magic.wizards.com/en/formats/commander-limited" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Commander Draft guidelines according to WotC</span></a>)</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>$55 entry, best of 1, single elimination. Event prizing to pods, additional prizing to winners + Top. <a href="https://topdeck.gg/event/commander-jam-2k26-legends-draft"><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Registration for the event is on TopDeck, right here!</span></a></em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>2:00 p.m. —</strong> 2HG and Planechase pods in-person signups open, first door prize drawings of the day!</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Sign up for Two-Headed Giant Commander and Planechase Pods<span style="color: #ffcc00;"> <a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://forms.gle/j6UDuNVu3YwCC1Ve7">via the Commanderjam Form</a></span> to guarantee your spot! </em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong> 2:30 p.m. —</strong> 2HG and Planechase pods fire</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>3:00 p.m. —</strong> Door prize drawings continue for everyone in-store, Commander pods form + fire as table space allows with special Commanderjam prize support. For folks interested in playing unaltered preconstructed decks and exhibition cEDH games, we’ll pair you up accordingly!</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Space on Commanderjam Saturday might be a little tougher to come by, and TGP staff are going to prioritize finding seating for groups playing MTG. We’re going to make sure there’s some additional space outside on the Alpha Pie patio for anyone who’d like to hang outdoors and play MTG al fresco, as well!</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><strong>4:00 p.m. —</strong> Deckbuilding Workshop sessions with Preston “Ironworks” Stevenson + friends open on a first-come, first-served basis. Possible guest-star inclusions for cEDH learn-to-play and other topics!</p>
<p><em>Want to get your name on the list to get deck building advice, critique, assistance, and whatever else? <span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://forms.gle/j6UDuNVu3YwCC1Ve7">Sign up here on the Commanderjam Form</a>!</span></em></p>
<p>You might have noticed there&#8217;s multiple spots attempting to direct you to the Commanderjam Form. It&#8217;s a Google Form, hopefully easy to understand + use + fill out. We want to use it as a way to get people in the games they want to day-of, as an estimation and pre-registration tool. To further incentivize folks making use of the form and helping us make Commanderjam as positively rad as possible, there are some FANTASTIC prizes up for grabs, drawings EXCLUSIVE to folks who fill out the form and show up for Commanderjam.</p>
<p>It should go more or less without saying, but you&#8217;ve got to be physically present at the event to claim your prize. You like fetchlands? You like bowmasters, of the orcish variety? You like playing Magic at TGP? Well dang, sounds like you better go fill out that form!</p>
<p>That&#8217;s a whole lot about Commanderjam, we&#8217;ve got to move on to other things for the week. See you Saturday, friends!</p>
<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="4505" data-permalink="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/05/16/commanderjam-2026-saturday-may-16/1-13/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?fit=1080%2C1350&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="1080,1350" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="1" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?fit=640%2C800&amp;ssl=1" class="aligncenter wp-image-4505 size-large" src="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?resize=640%2C800&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="640" height="800" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?resize=819%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 819w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?resize=240%2C300&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?resize=768%2C960&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/1.png?w=1080&amp;ssl=1 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></p>
<p>Tomorrow, Wednedsay, 5/13, is the monthly D&amp;D Learn to Play session. It starts at 6:00 p.m. and is helmed by your good friend and mine, Ben Creed! Usually these are on the first Wednesday of the month, but as you already know, we had to move it this go &#8217;round since Ben was in Vegas wheelin&#8217; and dealin&#8217; at MagicCon.</p>
<p>Secrets of Strixhaven continues to be a home run for MTG in more than one sense, and folks have been asking after boxes of boosters fairly often. We&#8217;ve still got a few boxes we&#8217;re holding for players to run Draft, so we&#8217;re going to put one last Secrets of Strixhaven Draft up for Friday Night Magic this week and &#8212; after that &#8212; all bets are off, at least until we get a restock.</p>
<p>Sunday is scheduled for the One Piece TCG Pirate&#8217;s Party, a rollicking good time with promos and high-seas shenanigans aplenty, and there&#8217;s more where that came from in terms of near-future events at The Gathering Place. To that end, click here to visit out Events Page and stay up-to-date on what&#8217;s happening at the shop.</p>
<p>Here&#8217;s what&#8217;s left in the month so far, since this already a pretty long Dispatch and we&#8217;re firmly at &#8220;in for a penny, in for a pound&#8221; territory:</p>
<hr />
<h3>Flesh and Blood Team Trios Tournament &amp; World Premiere Prague Watch Party</h3>
<p><em>Saturday, May 23, 12:00 p.m.</em></p>
<p>It&#8217;s an all-out FAB brawl at The Gathering Place! Saturday, May 23, starting at noon, we&#8217;re running a Team Trios tournament sure to knock the socks clean off all who dare step into the ring.</p>
<p>$20 buy in per player, each member of the team must use a different hero, prizing based on attendance. All three matches will be Classic Constructed, and we&#8217;ll have a FAB judge on hand. We&#8217;ll also tie this into putting the World Premiere FAB matches on the TVs over the tournament tables, so come hang!</p>
<p><a href="https://fabtcg.com/locator/the-gathering-place/"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
<h3>One Piece TCG Extra Grand Battle</h3>
<p><em>Sunday, May 24, 1:00 p.m.</em></p>
<p>Congratulations to One Piece for having made it into the hallowed halls of TCGs that need to introduce a historic format. As cards rotate out and the current meta shifts, One Piece Extra Grand Battle is a non-rotating all-time bangers way to play. TGP is running a tournament for EGB on Sunday, May 24, at 1:00 p.m. with $20 entry per player, pack and promo prizing, and the tournament will continue until there is a single undefeated player, an Extra Grand Champion!</p>
<p><a href="https://www.bandai-tcg-plus.com/event/6429173" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
<h3>Flesh and Blood: Omens of the Third Age Prerelease</h3>
<p><em>Friday, May 29, 7:30 p.m.</em></p>
<p>A new FAB release, a new Friday stacked with stuff!</p>
<p><a href="https://fabtcg.com/locator/the-gathering-place/"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
<h3>MTG Old School Cash Tournament (MTGPunks Series)</h3>
<p><em>Saturday, May 30, 12:00 p.m.</em></p>
<p>The MTGPunks tournament series at TGP is a monthly rotating cash tournament series of community-driven and fan-favorite formats for Magic.</p>
<p>May is Old School&#8217;s turn in the sun. We&#8217;re talking $30 entry! All Buy in going back into the prize pool! Old School at The Gathering Place, played using the <span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://www.eternalcentral.com/oldschool/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Eternal Central guidelines</a>! </span></p>
<p>Play Magic the way that Richard Garfield intended; with a nostalgic card pool from Alpha to Fallen Empires—where every deck is a time machine! Relive the aesthetics and power of iconic cards and strategic depth from &#8217;93-&#8217;94, all while embracing the charm of old-school gameplay.</p>
<p><a href="https://the-gathering-place.mybigcommerce.com/mtg-old-school-cash-tournament/"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
<h3>Riftbound Summoner&#8217;s Skirmish</h3>
<p><em>Sunday, May 31, 1:00 p.m.</em></p>
<p>Riftbound continues to be a hit at TGP and beyond, and we&#8217;ll be closing out May with another Summoner&#8217;s Skirmish!</p>
<p>This tournament will be run at a competitive rules enforcement level. 32 player maximum, $20 entry per player, Swiss rounds followed by a cut to top. If you&#8217;ve ever wanted to give serious competitive Riftbound play a shot, now&#8217;s your chance!</p>
<p><a href="https://locator.riftbound.uvsgames.com/events/409434"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
<hr />
</article><!-- #post-4622 -->                
<article class="tgp-post" id="post-4574">
	<h2>TGP Dispatch: 5/5/26</h2>	<div class="tgp-date-and-time">
		<div class="tgp-date">May 5, 2026</div>
		<div class="tgp-time">4:13 pm</div>
	</div>
			<div class="tgp-categories">
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/weekly-annoucements/tgp-dispatch/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					TGP Dispatch				</a>
							<a href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/category/weekly-annoucements/" class="tgp-category-chip">
					Weekly Annoucements				</a>
					</div>
		<hr />
	<p style="text-align: center;"><span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/events-page/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em><strong>TGP Events Page</strong></em></a></span></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jut0TLxHDOo1fQkL91lKqt-EmDBdwZ4QsUhhPHToCLY/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em><strong><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Monthly Calendar for The Gathering Place in Google Sheets</span></strong></em></a></p>
<hr />
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="4575" data-permalink="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/05/05/tgp-dispatch-5-5-26/dispatch-template-5/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template.png?fit=851%2C315&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="851,315" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="dispatch template" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template.png?fit=640%2C237&amp;ssl=1" class="aligncenter wp-image-4575 size-full" src="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template.png?resize=640%2C237&#038;ssl=1" alt="" width="640" height="237" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template.png?w=851&amp;ssl=1 851w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template.png?resize=300%2C111&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/gatheringplacegames.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/dispatch-template.png?resize=768%2C284&amp;ssl=1 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></p>
<hr />
<p>This week at The Gathering Place: the distro dungeon team is back from Vegas, we&#8217;re getting ready for a whole other round of conventions and shows, and we&#8217;ve got a slate of events and tournaments at the shop back to back to back!</p>
<p>First things first, this past weekend&#8217;s prerelease of Riftbound Unleashed really exceeded our expectations, and given how well people responded to running prerelease kits back for a supplementary event in the wake of Secrets of Strixhaven, we&#8217;re going to do the same thing this week! Wednesday, as in tomorrow, we&#8217;re going to have a Prerelease Part Two at TGP! <a href="https://locator.riftbound.uvsgames.com/events/545512" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Here&#8217;s the registration link</span></a>, and we&#8217;ll see you there.</p>
<p>Also this week, Thursday night will see the glorious and glittery return of Girlypop Magic at TGP! Another girlypop Commander night for the books, and we couldn&#8217;t be more stoked about it! We&#8217;ll have a table (or two, or three) reserved for GPM, any and all are welcome to join the festivities and the fray.</p>
<p>Speaking of Commander, <strong><span style="color: #ffcc00;"><a style="color: #ffcc00;" href="https://gatheringplacegames.com/2026/04/21/commanderjam-2026-saturday-may-16/">COMMANDERJAM is 11 days away</a></span></strong>! (click that link for all the details on this year&#8217;s Commander-focused party</p>
<p>But we can&#8217;t spend the whole dispatch dishing on Commanderjam. There&#8217;s a lot more to talk about. Specifically, since our own Ben Creed is fresh off the plane from sunny Las Vegas, the monthly D&amp;D Learn to Play session is formally scheduled for next Wednesday, 5/13.</p>
<p>In terms of what&#8217;s happening this weekend, it&#8217;s a doozy &#8212; not only is it graduation weekend here in Blue Heaven, but TGP has FOUR banner events on the calendar. Here&#8217;s the guide to each, taken straight from the TGP Events Page:</p>
<hr />
<h3>MTG Legacy Cash Tournament (Monthly MTG Series)</h3>
<p><em>Saturday, May 9, 12:00 p.m.</em></p>
<p>Spotlighting the <a href="https://magic.wizards.com/en/formats/legacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Legacy format</span></a>, this cash-payout MTG tournament has a buy-in of $30 to contribute to the prize pool, allows for 15 proxies in any given deck (proxies must be clearly representative of the intended card and contain all information the official printing does in an easy-to-identify fashion).</p>
<p>What&#8217;s the bonus prizing for this Legacy tournament? A freaking PLAYSET of LOTUS PETALS. Check &#8217;em out in the post below!</p>
<p><a href="https://the-gathering-place.mybigcommerce.com/events/mtg-legacy-cash-tournament/"><em><span style="color: #ffcc00;">Event Details + Registration</span></em></a></p>
